@startuml
title Expense submission — proposed layered flow (desktop and service use case)
actor Member
boundary "Swing View / Web-Mobile Client" as UI
control "ExpenseSubmissionService" as App
control "SplitCalculator" as Split
entity "Expense / Approval Policy" as Domain
database "ExpenseRepository" as Repo
collections "Notification outbox" as Outbox
Member -> UI: enter expense and submit
UI -> App: submit(command, authenticated context)
App -> Repo: load current group/membership
Repo --> App: authorized group snapshot
App -> Domain: validate fields, payer, participants, split
Domain --> App: valid / domain error
App -> Split: allocate(amount, method, ordered participants)
Split --> App: exact shares
App -> Repo: begin transaction
App -> Repo: save pending expense, shares, approval plan
App -> Outbox: enqueue recipient notices
App -> Repo: commit
App --> UI: pending result
UI --> Member: show pending state
Outbox --> App: asynchronous delivery handled by adapter
note over UI,App: UI collects/displays only; GUI-independent services own business rules.
@enduml
